WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
I made a bet on myself as an operator,

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.480
even though I had no business buying a

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:09.360
$50 million business.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.800
I made a bet on the fact that you can

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.240
hire remote teams all over the world

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.320
because I'm doing it. I have several of

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.840
my companies with zero plans to hire any

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.800
more Americans.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.400
Um and I'm making a bet on the fact that

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.600
the American worker is getting harder

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.480
and harder and more expensive and more

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.240
expensive to hire.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.360
So, if if two things are true is that

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.840
the United States worker will be in high

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.640
demand and will never be short of a job.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.040
That's one thing that I believe

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.320
fundamentally. There's enough work to do

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.800
in the United States that the Americans

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.400
can't do it all.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.840
Um if that's true

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.160
and it's true that you can build a

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:43.640
productive business using

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.040
employees in Bogota, Colombia, and

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.080
Johannesburg, South Africa, and Manila,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.360
Philippines, if that's also true,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.480
then

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.920
the demand for what we do at Somewhere

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.200
will be massive.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.440
Um and I know both of them to be true

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.400
because I experienced it in my other

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.520
businesses. Mhm. Now, that third one,

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.880
can I do it? Can Nick Huber do it? Can I

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.960
Am I the operator who can take that

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:06.920
business to the next level?

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.920
That remains to be seen.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.000
I I I'd love to just talk a little bit

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.640
about like the um

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.760
the sales the sales bets that you've

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.320
made operationally and how you put your

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.360
finger on South Africa. How did South

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.480
Africa get on your radar?

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.840
I had a guy DM me about a year ago.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:26.440
Um and he said, "Nick, I'm a I'm a

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.120
growth marketer.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.320
I live in Cape Town. I want to work with

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.360
one of your companies." And he came in

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.400
and he started working for my media

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.840
company and and moving a lot of things

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.520
around. I'm like, "Wow,

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.200
this guy's super switched on. He can

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.840
lead teams.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.280
Um it's like I hired somebody from New

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.760
York City, but I pay him four grand a

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.800
month instead of,

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:47.480
you know, 40 or whatever it would take

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.400
for somebody at that level."

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.800
So, then I

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:54.560
hired a sales person

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.120
through somewhere.com into Bolt Storage

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.440
and I started watching that funnel that

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.200
we're talking about of watching the

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.000
number of calls, listening to the

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.520
conversations, looking at the

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.120
conversions, and all of a sudden I had

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.720
one of my reps that was closing new

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.400
storage calls

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.679
at 45% when everybody else was closing

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:12.480
at 28%.

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:13.600
Now, when you own $120 million worth of

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.920
storage

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.880
and you're leasing 15,000 units, and

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.560
you're fielding 200 phone calls per day,

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:22.880
and you're paying $100 per phone call

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.880
for those for the phone to ring,

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.800
if somebody can close 45% instead of 28,

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.360
alarm bells start going off in your

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.280
head. Why? Why? Why? Why? And I started

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.720
listening to the conversations. I

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.320
started listening to my South African

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.040
sales rep talking to rural American

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.959
clients.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.920
And I started listening to my Filipino

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:42.880
reps talk to

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:46.040
rural American clients. And

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.400
as soon as my Filipino reps said hello

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.480
and introduced themselves, and they're

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.320
great, and we still have some. They're

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.760
amazing on our team. As soon as people

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.040
heard the accent, the Tagalog accent

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.520
that is in the United that is in the

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.080
Philippines,

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.080
many of them, not all of them, many of

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.280
them got disrespectful, many of them got

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.519
a shorter temper, many of them just knew

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.920
that they were talking to somebody on

00:03:03.519 --> 00:03:06.720
the other side of the world. They were

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.800
used to like press four on the Bank of

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:11.360
America call line, right?

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.640
Right. When they were talking to my

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.360
South African rep with the

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.280
British accent,

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.440
um

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.680
it was a lively conversation. They were

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.280
asking them where in the United States

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.320
they live and if they're from England.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.600
They're asking them if they were from

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.480
Australia.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.360
Um there was a different level of

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.800
respect and regard for my reps. Now,

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:32.560
what that says about America is a little

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:34.640
bit sad, but

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:37.000
it was clear that

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.280
also my South Africans had a a culture

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.519
of sales. They weren't afraid to be

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.440
pushy. They were not afraid to put

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:43.040
themselves out there. They were not

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.600
afraid of rejection.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.840
A a slight cultural difference. And now,

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.800
that's not the same for every rep,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.080
obviously, but I had somebody whose

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:52.200
English as a first language,

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.440
a smooth British accent or African

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.880
accent, which is also European and I had

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.600
higher close rates.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:00.080
So alarm bells are going off in my head.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.040
Holy cow, if I do this across my entire

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.120
organization, we're going to lease more

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:04.680
units

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.360
and my entire portfolio is going to add

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:09.959
millions of dollars of value.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:11.840
And so we turned the switch and we hired

00:04:09.959 --> 00:04:13.200
a head of sales who was a chief revenue

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:15.480
officer at a company and had built a

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.040
sales team of 15 people, hired him for

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.680
$4,500 a month base plus commission.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:22.560
Where that hire in the United States is

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:24.160
$200,000 $250,000 a year hire.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.960
Started hiring high ticket closers at

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.240
somewhere.com. If you set up a call at

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.720
somewhere.com, you'll listen to one of

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.080
my high ticket closers in South Africa

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.120
talk to you.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.600
Two grand a month base, another thousand

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.640
to 1500 commission where we're looking

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:37.360
at 200 grand a year again for a high

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:39.520
ticket salesperson in the United States,

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.680
a closer, an account executive.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.440
Um so it started to change the way I

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.600
think about sales. And

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.840
sales sales talent is the hardest most

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.320
expensive talent to hire in the United

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.600
States, period.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:52.840
So and the second thing I found out

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.880
about South Africa is that 30,000 South

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:57.520
Africans every single year get on

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.880
airplanes and go to New York City, DC

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:02.200
and work in Fortune 500 companies on tax

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:04.200
and audit during the busy season.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:07.120
Chartered accountant is like the doctor

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.720
and lawyer of South Africa. Every mom

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.240
wants their son or daughter to grow up

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.600
to be a chartered accountant and go work

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.640
for Deloitte or Price Waterhouse Cooper,

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:13.840
whoever else in the United States. Got

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:14.960
it.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.600
>> It's a massive culture these people that

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:20.240
go back and want to work remote as

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.120
controllers, as bookkeepers, as accounts

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:23.880
for US based businesses

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:25.160
for three to five K a month.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:28.320
When that same hire in the United States

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:28.320
is 150 grand a year.

